From 582907012b95cc4821fc160c93ea9601b8d3be84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WS-P <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:32:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] redfin: TSENS temperatures (SWEET THERMAL) and boot PM7250B
 charger/gauge register dump

sweet_thermal.c samples both TSENS controllers read-only every 5 s
(sysctl kern.sweet_temp_*), logs the SMB5/QG/SDAM registers once at
boot; the SPMI read allow-list gains peripherals 0x15, 0x16, 0xb1.
Boot-arg sweettherm=0: off.
---
 bsd/conf/files          |   1 +
 bsd/dev/sweet_cpufreq.c |   2 +
 bsd/dev/sweet_spmi.c    |   4 +-
 bsd/dev/sweet_thermal.c | 259 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 265 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 bsd/dev/sweet_thermal.c

